            <ArticleTitle>[Subclavian steal-carotid recovery phenomenon - &quot;old school&quot; surgical procedure].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>306-308</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Subclavian steal-carotid recovery phenomenon appears to be related to the occlusion of the truncus brachiocephalicus and can be a rare cause of neurological deficit. In this syndrome, the right common carotid artery and right subclavian artery are filled with retrograde flow from the ipsilateral vertebral artery. We present a patient with this type of steal syndrome managed by a classical surgical procedure for stent reocclusion in the truncus brachiocephalicus.Key words: steal phenomenon endarterectomy truncus brachiocephalicus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
